IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-cpc-interface`
IMPORT `ea-types`
IMPORT `ea-parol-evidence`

-- Tests for ea-parol-evidence.l4 (Evidence Act 1893, ss 93 to 102).
-- Expected values are read off the Act's text and illustrations.  Generated by generators/ea_tests_2.py.

`s93 ill a contract in letters` MEANS `Parol Evidence Facts` WITH
    `the terms of a contract, grant or other disposition of property have been reduced by or by consent of the parties to the form of a document` IS TRUE
    `the matter is required by law to be reduced to the form of a document` IS FALSE
    `a public officer is required by law to be appointed in writing and it is shown that a particular person has acted as such officer` IS FALSE
    `the will has been admitted to probate in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the fact to be proved is a fact other than the terms of the contract, grant or disposition, or the matter, required to be in a document` IS FALSE
    `the terms of the document have been proved according to section 93` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of an oral agreement or statement` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is offered as between the parties to the instrument or their representatives in interest` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is for the purpose of contradicting, varying, adding to or subtracting from the terms of the document` IS FALSE
    `the fact would invalidate the document or entitle a person to a decree or order relating to it` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a separate oral agreement as to a matter on which the document is silent and which is not inconsistent with its terms` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a separate oral agreement constituting a condition precedent to the attaching of an obligation under the document` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a distinct subsequent oral agreement to rescind or modify the contract, grant or disposition` IS FALSE
    `the contract, grant or disposition is by law required to be in writing, or has been registered according to the law in force as to the registration of documents` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a usage or custom by which incidents not expressly mentioned in a contract are usually annexed to contracts of that description` IS FALSE
    `annexing the incident would be repugnant to or inconsistent with the express terms of the contract` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a fact which shows in what manner the language of the document is related to existing facts` IS FALSE
    `the language used in the document is on its face ambiguous or defective` IS FALSE
    `the language used in the document is plain in itself and applies accurately to existing facts` IS FALSE
    `the language used in the document is plain in itself but meaningless in reference to existing facts` IS FALSE
    `the language might have been meant to apply to any one, and could not have been meant to apply to more than one, of several persons or things` IS FALSE
    `the language applies partly to one set of existing facts and partly to another, and the whole of it does not apply correctly to either` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is to show the meaning of illegible or not commonly intelligible characters, or of foreign, obsolete, technical, local or provincial expressions, abbreviations or words used in a peculiar sense` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is given by a person who is not a party to the document or a representative in interest of a party` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a fact tending to show a contemporaneous agreement varying the terms of the document` IS FALSE
    `the question is as to the construction of a will` IS FALSE

